-- Window toggle: RightControl | Panic: End | API: getgenv().RobScriptGrowAnomaly
--
-- How the farm works: this game breaks blocks when the anomaly swings at them.
-- The attack button only sends AnomalyAttackEvent to the server, so the loop below
-- stands the character right in front of a destructible block, turns it towards that
-- block and sends the same remote at the game's own attack cooldown. The server carves
-- the block in front of the character (the client version of that carve lives in
-- ReplicatedStorage.Shared.Modules.Destruction) and pays mass for the carved volume.
--
-- The character is placed by CFrame instead of walking: the game's controller clears
-- the humanoid input every frame, so MoveTo and Move do nothing, and the Climbing
-- state keeps the character glued to trunks. Placing the character is instant and the
-- server still accepts the swing, which is why one block costs one attack cooldown.

